On the Origins of SelfModeling,2020,LaTeX_Sources_Recovered/1_Core_Self_Modeling/On the Origins of SelfModeling,"Self-Modeling is the process by which an agent, such as an animal or machine, learns to create a predictive model of its own dynamics. Once captured, this self-model can then allow the agent to plan and evaluate various potential behaviors internally using the self-model, rather than using costly physical experimentation.",No numerical results found
